Torchlight: RTSS sphere and reflection environment maps as Runic's RT Shader System
library computes them (the Xbox build's rtshaderlib/FFPLib_Texturing.hlsl).
FFP_GenerateTexCoord_EnvMap_Sphere maps the view-space normal itself onto the
sphere map, (n.x/2 + 0.5, -n.y/2 + 0.5), through the world and view matrices
and not normalised; OGRE 14 maps a reflection vector. The characters' render-
behind outline (outlineblue.dds, ENV_CURVED; CGenericModel::reInitialize
) samples it, and the captured console frame shows the Runic
form. FFP_GenerateTexCoord_EnvMap_Reflect: Runic does not normalise the
normal. Not __SWITCH__-guarded (a GLSL library file; both targets need it).


diff --git a/Media/RTShaderLib/FFPLib_Texturing.glsl b/Media/RTShaderLib/FFPLib_Texturing.glsl
index 827307373..c6bce8a6e 100644
--- a/Media/RTShaderLib/FFPLib_Texturing.glsl
+++ b/Media/RTShaderLib/FFPLib_Texturing.glsl
@@ -70,12 +70,13 @@ void FFP_GenerateTexCoord_EnvMap_Sphere(in 	mat4 mWorldView,
 										in 	vec3 vNormal,
 										out vec2 vOut)
 {
-	vec3 normal = normalize( mul(mWorldIT, vNormal));
-	vec3 eyedir =  normalize(mul(mWorldView, vPos)).xyz;
-	vec3 r = reflect(eyedir, normal);
-	r.z += 1.0;
-	float two_p = 2.0 * length(r);
-	vOut = vec2(0.5 + r.x / two_p, 0.5 - r.y / two_p);
+	// Torchlight port: Runic's RT Shader System library (the Xbox build's
+	// rtshaderlib/FFPLib_Texturing.hlsl, FFP_GenerateTexCoord_EnvMap_Sphere)
+	// maps the view-space normal itself, through the world and view matrices
+	// (not their inverse transpose) and not normalised, onto the sphere map:
+	// the characters' render-behind outline (outlineblue.dds) samples it so.
+	vec3 vViewNormal = mul(mWorldView, vec4(vNormal, 0.0)).xyz;
+	vOut = vec2(vViewNormal.x * 0.5 + 0.5, -vViewNormal.y * 0.5 + 0.5);
 }
 
